1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,080
You had a tail.

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:02,480
A real one.

3
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,380
Guess when.

4
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,000
Week five...

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,880
in the womb.

6
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,500
About a sixth of your whole body.

7
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,580
By week eight, gone.

8
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,900
The tail cells died off and got

9
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:14,400
cleared away.

10
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:17,220
Apes lost theirs too, about twenty

11
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:18,480
-five million years ago.

12
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,980
In 2024, scientists found a suspect.

13
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,860
A jumping gene that landed inside a

14
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:27,140
tail gene called T B X T.

15
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,760
Recreate its effect in mice...

16
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,820
and they're born with short tails, or

17
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:32,440
none at all.

18
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:35,000
But some of those mice also had spine

19
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,100
defects, like spina bifida.

20
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,640
So the researchers suspect losing the

21
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,460
tail came with a price...

22
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:42,740
one we may still be paying.

23
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,260
And it's not junk.

24
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:46,480
Muscles anchor to what's left.

25
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:49,160
Right now, you're sitting on it...

26
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,620
the tail you already had.
